Subject: Nightingale Update - Priority One

Agent Kepler,

Received your comm regarding the Bucharest anomaly. Confirmed. The “collector” – designation “Silas Thorne” – is legitimate. He isn’t after antiquities, as the initial reports suggested. He’s building something. Specifically, a resonance amplifier. Preliminary scans indicate it’s designed to exploit the Leyden frequencies – the same ones we detected near the Svalbard seed vault. A concerning overlap.

Thorne is operating under the guise of a rare book dealer, but his “collection” is almost entirely focused on texts detailing pre-Roman Balkan metallurgy and obscure alchemical treatises. He’s not *reading* them, he’s dismantling them, extracting specific alloys and diagrams. We’ve intercepted shipments of refined Tellurium and a surprisingly large quantity of naturally occurring Yttrium. These aren’t components for bookbinding.

The location – the abandoned textile mill outside Bucharest – is heavily shielded. Standard surveillance is useless. I’ve managed to plant a micro-drone, disguised as a moth, but its range is limited and the signal is degraded. It confirms the presence of at least six heavily armed guards, rotating shifts, and a central chamber where the majority of the construction is taking place. The chamber is lined with a strange, dark metal – analysis pending, but it doesn’t match any known alloy. 

My current assessment is that Thorne intends to amplify the Leyden frequencies to… well, we don’t know exactly. The potential applications are terrifying. Everything from localized EMP bursts to, theoretically, manipulating tectonic plates. The Svalbard connection suggests he’s interested in accessing or disrupting something *within* the seed vault. We need to determine what.

I’ve established a contact within the Romanian intelligence service – code name “Raven” – but he’s cautious. He’s aware of Thorne’s activities, but believes it’s a smuggling operation. I’m working to convince him of the larger threat, but it’s slow going. 

Requesting immediate authorization for a full infiltration team. We need to secure the amplifier and any data related to the Svalbard connection. I can provide a detailed schematic of the mill’s layout, based on the drone’s limited scans. Also, prioritize analysis of the dark metal. Its composition could be key to understanding Thorne’s ultimate goal. 

Time is critical. The amplifier is nearing completion. I estimate operational readiness within 72 hours. 

Await your orders.

Nightingale.



